Subject: [PATCH 2/6] B20_R10: custodian statement screen for research, checker
 CPU metering, error lines kept in checker logs

* custodian.screen_statements_for_research: signed ALLOW/BLOCK decisions against every statement
  sealed at the custodian (partition relations; salted commitment; private ledger; no reserved text);
  partitions.CustodianStatementScreen (verifies the receipt, fails closed) and partitions.both (B20R7-OPEN-2).
* fof_lean.replay / custody.replay_target report the checker's cgroup CPU (cached modules count 0);
  statement replay attempts carry it (B20R7-OPEN-1).
* checker._kept_log: error lines first, then the tail, when a module log exceeds 6000 characters
  (B20R3-OPEN-3). Diagnostics only; the replay route's identity changes (translator and checker files).
* Tests: ResearchScreen (statement custody), KeptLog (formal), CPU assertions in replay and statement tests.

